{"decisions":[{"i":0,"decision":"F2","origin":"compose","reason":"In Dutch, “quadriljoen” denotes 10^24, while the source’s “quadrillion” is 10^15; the article therefore overstates the quantity by a factor of 10^9.","sourceEvidence":"The source reports 42.4 out of 605.6 quadrillion Btu for total energy production.","synthesisStatement":"Across all energy production, renewables were 42.4 out of 605.6 quadrillion Btu, reported as 7%.","narrativeStatement":"Across all energy production, renewables were 42.4 out of 605.6 quadrillion Btu, reported as 7%.","materiality":"The unit translation changes the stated scale by nine orders of magnitude."}]}

